                "Championed radical Nirguna monotheism: 'Allah and Ram are one and the same'.",
                "Fiercely ridiculed idol worship, ritual bathing, animal sacrifice, caste divisions, and clerical dogmatism.",
                "Wrote in Sadhukkari (Khari Boli mixed dialect) using Dohas (Sakhis), Sabads, and Ulatbansi (inverted riddles).",
                "The Bijak is the canonical collection of Kabir's poetry, compiled by Dharam Das.",
                "The Guru Granth Sahib includes 541 hymns of Kabir.",
                "Died at Maghar to demolish the superstition that salvation depended on dying in Varanasi."
